# A load-bearing security control, not housekeeping — a stray local .env or
# credential file baked into an image layer is a real and common accident.
# Docker's exclusion patterns, unlike git's, only match at the context root
# unless prefixed with **/ — every entry here is **/-prefixed so a nested
# .env or key file (e.g. sub/.env, certs/fmc-ca.pem) is excluded too, not
# just one at the repo root.
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.env
!example.env
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*.crt
**/*.p12

.git
node_modules
dist
.claude

.scratch
data
test
docs
*.md
